#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133696 :question/id #uuid "ac6e7a2c-19a3-595a-ba46-f38c653a9bec" :question/math-academy-id "e-8927" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d37f2a445986b2aae60603fed3bef1b480d8f049dfe17a0cf26325ac2eb167d8.png)\n\n \n\nConsider the vector field $\\mathbf F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $\\mathbf F?$\n\nI. $\\textrm{div}\\,\\mathbf F = 0$\n\nII. $\\textrm{div}\\,\\mathbf F > 0$\n\nIII. $\\textrm{div}\\,\\mathbf F <                    0$\n\nIV. $\\mathbf F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\textrm{div}\\, \\mathbf F = \\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $\\mathbf F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $\\mathbf F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $\\mathbf F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n- If $\\mathbf F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $\\nabla \\cdot  \\mathbf F > 0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $\\mathbf F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $\\nabla \\cdot  \\mathbf F <         0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $\\mathbf F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $\\nabla \\cdot  \\mathbf F =0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F = 0$ everywhere in the domain of $\\mathbf F,$ we say that $\\mathbf F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statements II and III are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $\\mathbf F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F = 0$ everywhere, the vector field $\\mathbf F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048917 :topic/math-academy-id 3344 :topic/title "Visualizing Vector Fields"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a764f49-9edb-5020-9a41-bf5dac3e103e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130523} {:answer/id #uuid "9d6d6769-d8ff-5808-9fdc-2c6a3c27f2ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130524} {:answer/id #uuid "e1924edf-bb90-519c-ad15-dc5c4909ac55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130525} {:answer/id #uuid "080a320c-3361-5001-ab96-5c073de14d26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130526} {:answer/id #uuid "1145c273-7eaa-577b-8a14-75a420c86885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130527}] :answer-field/id #uuid "39063289-e948-5c53-bc32-a9e7fa1b008c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130522} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af00ead-cb31-51e6-9f21-869070b74a3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382717} {:answer/id #uuid "5e82f46c-d873-514d-bfa9-fcd50b8798f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382718} {:answer/id #uuid "57566773-e704-586b-bc5c-d48eca074e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382719} {:answer/id #uuid "b43f392a-de66-542d-85c1-a5e456a297d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382720} {:answer/id #uuid "a163be0a-2b14-51bd-a9a8-1d4a4207b41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b43f392a-de66-542d-85c1-a5e456a297d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382720} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bcce67f-0a6c-5ff1-abd8-5204a040f9e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382716}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d82a128a-970f-55e8-b4ad-4c3c16a14935" :question/math-academy-id "q-105075" :question/problem "![](images/34/3411e11060b06a11c82ad677f50731faa31c6bc2e83ccb0d0d10931cf3d76592.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $\\text{div}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F>0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P,$ then $F$ acts like a source at $P.$\n\n- If $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P,$ then $F$ acts like a sink at $P.$\n\n- If $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P,$ then $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement III is true, whereas statements I and II are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors decrease as we move in the $y$-direction. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a sink at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "869bd612-bbbc-56b2-9d4d-f34bcb0e9062" :answe