s/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statements II and III are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "293fea52-e929-5811-afed-af97ddebf14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238420} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc29659-6ed2-5300-9382-238c0d2c4601" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239277} {:answer/id #uuid "9d34961c-bb25-5812-86f9-33a7d799bc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239424} {:answer/id #uuid "c71effce-e296-5a41-bbf5-5519f9760ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239809} {:answer/id #uuid "f28361df-fd6a-50c5-8758-cfb0d1e00173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "293fea52-e929-5811-afed-af97ddebf14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238420} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bea141b-d468-560c-9266-a844ba797d87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240410}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2be15a89-9d36-55d5-9fa3-9993a8ff3b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105578" :question/problem "![](images/33/33f0353e3856fb2b458d17ed1959918e6a3dd96fd0a966d971575ffc212402f0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $\\text{div}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F>0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move horizontally and vertically away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336f3f9e-6053-5a86-b639-96673bb8f672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257234} {:answer/id #uuid "39162a94-0d90-5b25-b209-24876a170a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257285} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8b15ca-d52d-531a-9f40-45fe63da8575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257571} {:answer/id #uuid "5c64bab9-76fe-5d95-8daf-e8e1b620127c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257585} {:answer/id #uuid "a0382c8f-1bdd-5f43-bb7f-8f4cbd016ed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39162a94-0d90-5b25-b209-24876a170a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257285} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0c79f3-5071-5ae2-996b-25bb19951a62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259478}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d890a9be-d244-5a2b-a434-390b31123a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-123245" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b315be9ba524ab538388fdaad31161c280d7d6e5ab71261345063ac6ffe819d5.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $∇\\cdot F=0$\n- $∇\\cdot F>0$\n- $∇\\cdot F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move vertically and horizontally away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ba8325-0de5-55e0-b591-b13e3cdf4ce5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263214} {:answer/id #uuid "9a082c1d-14e4-53ff-92d2-66ed283dd413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264320} {:answer/id #uuid "9fad71dc-b40f-5c4c-bb22-8e3334af0c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264360} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e9170b-f2b7-5b98-8476-275056448f80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264711} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d0c06d-23f7-52e0-b017-3b762a830f93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fad71dc-b40f-5c4c-bb22-8e3334af0c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264360} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea5cca5b-3f01-52ef-89bb-4b92a787b6ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265660}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48d2c508-8f65-5677-91ea-4bbc2f84d34b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131192" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e30919dc7cc107bdda9872079b4dc0e59fe8e3e5767aa2d407b9d0af392803e0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $\\text{div}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F>0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vector's $y$-components increase as we move vertically away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266063 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24e3d2fa-2512-5462-9398-2a405f6d7d67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263317} {:answer/id #uuid "5a0b785a-0eb8-57a0-825a-938a683bad1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263776} {:answer/id #uuid "8820c9da-a52e-5b7c-8e1b-89811eeef148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264175} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9b9b35-f09b-5b88-9a8b-3096512d0b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264185} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a018d7-e9e5-5ca8-9567-308f5666fcc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a0b785a-0eb8-57a0-825a-938a683bad1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263776} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d7511c4-3f39-553d-b99b-12a596c766ac" :answer